  "annotations": [
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Bottomed their only Mountain from a hand that needs red mana for every spell. With only Soulstone Sanctuary (colorless mana) remaining as a land, they cannot cast any spell in their hand - Burnout Bashtronaut needs R, Shock needs R, Razorkin Needlehead needs RR. They're essentially starting the game with 0 castable cards until they draw a Mountain.",
      "action_taken": "Bottomed Mountain, leaving only Soulstone Sanctuary as their single land producing only colorless mana.",
      "better_line": "Bottom a duplicate Razorkin Needlehead or Nova Hellkite. Keeping the Mountain is critical to have any red mana source to cast the aggressive creatures in hand.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 2,
      "player": "Haiku Villain",
      "decision_index": 3,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Playing Steam Vents on turn 1 instead of Rockface Village means either paying 2 life unnecessarily to cast Hired Claw, or having the land enter tapped and missing the turn 1 Hired Claw play. Rockface Village enters untapped for free and can tap for {R} to cast creature spells like Hired Claw.",
      "action_taken": "Played Steam Vents as turn 1 land",
      "better_line": "Play Rockface Village turn 1 (enters untapped, taps for {R} for creatures), cast Hired Claw. Play Steam Vents turn 2 (can enter tapped to save life, still have 2 mana for Lightning Strike if needed).",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 7,
      "player": "Haiku Villain",
      "decision_index": 10,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "With 2 mana available (Steam Vents untapped + Rockface Village, though Rockface Village can only add R for creatures), the player could cast a second Hired Claw for just {R} to develop the board further. Having two Hired Claws means the attack trigger deals 2 damage instead of 1 when attacking with Lizards, accelerating the clock significantly. Passing with mana unused on turn 2 when there's a cheap creature to deploy is wasteful tempo.",
      "action_taken": "Passed without casting anything, leaving mana unused.",
      "better_line": "Cast the second Hired Claw for {R} using Rockface Village's creature-mana ability, developing the board and doubling the Lizard attack trigger damage.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 20,
      "player": "Haiku Villain",
      "decision_index": 15,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Failed to activate Hired Claw's +1/+1 counter ability when the condition was met (opponent lost life this turn, going to 19). Had the mana available (Steam Vents + Rockface Village for {1}{R}) and no better use for the mana with an empty opposing board.",
      "action_taken": "Passed without activating Hired Claw's ability, leaving mana unused.",
      "better_line": "Activate Hired Claw's {1}{R} ability to put a +1/+1 counter on it, making it a 2/3 permanently. There was no reason to hold up mana with the opponent having only a Starting Town and no board presence.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 22,
      "player": "Haiku Villain",
      "decision_index": 18,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Missed the opportunity to activate Hired Claw's pump ability ({1}{R}: Put a +1/+1 counter) during combat. The opponent already lost 1 life from Hired Claw's attack trigger, enabling the ability. A permanent +1/+1 counter making it a 2/3 would be significant value for an aggressive deck, especially since the mana would otherwise go unused this turn.",
      "action_taken": "Passed without activating Hired Claw's pump ability or casting any spells.",
      "better_line": "Activate Hired Claw's +1/+1 counter ability using Steam Vents and Rockface Village, permanently making it a 2/3. This uses mana that would otherwise be wasted and creates a much more threatening attacker for future turns.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 23,
      "player": "Haiku Villain",
      "decision_index": 19,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Hired Claw's ability says '{1}{R}: Put a +1/+1 counter on this creature. Activate only if an opponent lost life this turn and only once each turn.' The opponent has lost life this turn (went from 19 to 18 from Hired Claw's trigger damage), so this ability is now active. With Rockface Village and Steam Vents available (providing {R} and another mana), the player could have activated Hired Claw's ability to put a +1/+1 counter on it, making it a 2/3. This is a free permanent buff that was missed.",
      "action_taken": "Passed without activating Hired Claw's +1/+1 counter ability.",
      "better_line": "Activate Hired Claw's {1}{R} ability using Steam Vents and Rockface Village to put a +1/+1 counter on it, permanently growing it to a 2/3.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 24,
      "player": "Haiku Villain",
      "decision_index": 20,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Paid 2 life for Hallowed Fountain to enter untapped when Floodfarm Verge would have accomplished the same thing for free. Both lands enable casting Llanowar Elves this turn (using Starting Town for G). Against an aggressive deck with two Hired Claws, 2 life matters. Floodfarm Verge now and Hallowed Fountain later (when it might need to enter untapped for a specific play) is strictly better sequencing.",
      "action_taken": "Played Hallowed Fountain paying 2 life to enter untapped",
      "better_line": "Play Floodfarm Verge (enters untapped, taps for W), then use Starting Town to pay 1 life for G to cast Llanowar Elves. Save Hallowed Fountain for a later turn.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 30,
      "player": "MiMo Spike",
      "decision_index": 23,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "The Hired Claws have already attacked and dealt their trigger damage, and the opponent is at 15 life (meaning an opponent has lost life this turn). Both Hired Claws have the activated ability '{1}{R}: Put a +1/+1 counter on this creature. Activate only if an opponent lost life this turn and only once each turn.' The opponent has an empty board with no blockers, so the Hired Claws are attacking unblocked. Pumping them before damage resolves would deal extra damage. With 3 untapped lands (Steam Vents, Rockface Village, Mountain), they could activate at least one Hired Claw's ability to put a +1/+1 counter on it, making it a 2/3 that deals 2 damage instead of 1. They might even be able to activate both if they have enough mana (each costs {1}{R}, so they'd need 4 mana total but only have 3 lands). They could activate one for sure, dealing 1 extra damage.",
      "action_taken": "Passed without activating any Hired Claw pump abilities before combat damage.",
      "better_line": "Activate one Hired Claw's +1/+1 counter ability for {1}{R} before combat damage resolves, dealing an extra 1 point of combat damage (total 3 instead of 2 from creatures).",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 43,
      "player": "Haiku Villain",
      "decision_index": 30,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "After attacking with both Hired Claws and dealing combat damage, the opponent lost life this turn. Hired Claw's activated ability '{1}{R}: Put a +1/+1 counter on this creature. Activate only if an opponent lost life this turn and only once each turn' could be activated on one of the Hired Claws. With a Mountain and Rockface Village available (assuming at least one is untapped), spending {1}{R} to put a +1/+1 counter on a Hired Claw would grow it for future attacks. The player declined to use this pure-upside mana sink.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without activating Hired Claw's +1/+1 counter ability.",
      "better_line": "Activate one Hired Claw's ability for {1}{R} to put a +1/+1 counter on it, making it a 2/3 for future attacks. The opponent has lost life this turn from combat damage, so the condition is met.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 44,
      "player": "Haiku Villain",
      "decision_index": 31,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "With the opponent having already lost life this turn from Hired Claw attack triggers, the Hired Claw's +1/+1 counter ability could be activated for {1}{R}. With Steam Vents and Mountain available, pumping one Hired Claw before combat damage would deal an extra 1 damage to the opponent (from 4 total to 5 total). This is a free permanent buff, not just until end of turn.",
      "action_taken": "Passed without activating any Hired Claw pump abilities, dealing only 4 damage total.",
      "better_line": "Activate one Hired Claw's {1}{R} ability to put a permanent +1/+1 counter on it, dealing 5 damage total this combat and having a bigger creature going forward.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 45,
      "player": "Haiku Villain",
      "decision_index": 32,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "After combat damage, Haiku Villain has the opportunity to activate Hired Claw's +1/+1 counter ability ({1}{R}: Put a +1/+1 counter on this creature, activate only if an opponent lost life this turn). The opponent just took combat damage this turn, so the condition is met. With 3 lands available (Steam Vents, Rockface Village, Mountain), they could activate one Hired Claw's ability for {1}{R}, growing it from 1/2 to 2/3. This is a free advantage that costs no cards and makes future attacks better.",
      "action_taken": "Passed without activating Hired Claw's +1/+1 counter ability after combat damage.",
      "better_line": "Activate one Hired Claw's {1}{R} ability to put a +1/+1 counter on it, since an opponent lost life this turn. This grows it permanently at no card cost.",
